# SoMe Benchmark Reproduction: Misinformation Detection (MID) Task

This repository contains the Misinformation Detection (MID) task from the [SoMe Benchmark](https://github.com/LivXue/SoMe) and introduced an anti-hallucination prompt to mitigate tool-use hallucinations.

## 🛠️ Modifications Made
- **Model Swapped**: Replaced the default Llama model with `qwen2.5-7b-instruct` via Alibaba Cloud DashScope API.
- **Data Pruning**: Bypassed the ~50GB `.npy` database loading by creating dummy files, reducing memory usage to a few megabytes to prevent OOM errors in Google Colab.
- **Bug Fixes**: Fixed `ModuleNotFoundError` by correctly routing the HTTP requests, and resolved an infinite loop caused by hidden `FileNotFoundError` exceptions by adding robust `os.makedirs` logic.
- **Anti-Hallucination Policy**: Injected strictly scoped rules (`NO RETRIES` and `NO GUESSING`) into the agent's system prompt to force it to acknowledge database errors rather than hallucinating answers.

